LICENSE IDEA

The person who wrote this license saw a problem with open source, namely a motivational one — with open code, a project can easily be stolen without credit being given to the author. Because of this, developers often burn out when they see a consumerist attitude. Therefore, under WAKE, the author has the ability to keep the source code closed during the development stage and is required to enable monetization, protecting themselves from the free-labor syndrome. Value your work fairly — if you become too greedy, the market itself will stop your sales.

There is also a piece of pragmatism. If the author no longer uses the code and no longer develops the project — it is more logical to make it open, but authorship still remains with them. Abandoned work should not die on hard drives.

Authorship is not a formality to us. It cannot be bought, taken away together with the files, erased with a single edit, or voluntarily abandoned. The creator's name remains alongside their work, wherever it may end up. We value your efforts.

The license is based on three principles:

First — The Author always remains the Author. Their name is preserved everywhere their work lives. The Author must respect themselves, therefore voluntarily abandoning their name or prematurely transferring the project into the public domain is strictly prohibited.

Second — Work should provide a return. While the project is being created, the Author must remind the world that there is a living person behind the code who requires support.

Third — Abandoned work should not disappear. If the Author abandons the project, the code returns to the people so that it can be studied and developed further, while the creator's name remains attached to it.

WHAT WE ARE TALKING ABOUT (DEFINITIONS)

Author — the person who created the Project.

Project — software, source code, binary files, documentation, and everything else distributed under this License.

Source Code — the form of the Project that is most convenient for studying and modifying.

Derivative Work — anything you have created based on the Project or that substantially incorporates it or its Source Code.

Update — a release of a new version of the Project containing critical vulnerability fixes, bug fixes, core refactoring, or the addition of new functionality (Significant Update). Changing the date, version number, metadata, comments, folder structure, documentation files (including README or the License text) does not constitute an Update and does not reset the abandonment timer.

Active Development — the Project is being developed or maintained by the Author or someone entrusted with it by the Author, with regular releases of meaningful Updates.

Abandoned Project — a Project that:
A) the Author has personally declared abandoned, or
B) has not received Updates for 2 consecutive years.

WHAT YOU MAY DO

The Author grants everyone a worldwide, non-exclusive right, provided that you comply with this License, to:

use and run the Project;
copy it;
study it, if the Source Code is open;
modify it and create Derivative Works within the scope of this License;
distribute the Project and permitted Derivative Works.

SOURCE CODE AND MONETIZATION WHILE THE PROJECT IS ALIVE

While Active Development is ongoing, the Author is not required to disclose the Source Code and may distribute the Project only in ready-to-use, compiled form (as binaries).

The Author MUST enable and maintain working channels for financial support (links to donations, cryptocurrency wallets, or donation platforms). Distribution of the Project without an opportunity to support the Author is prohibited under the terms of WAKE. Selling ready-made compiled builds of the Project for money is a fully permitted option and remains at the sole discretion of the Author.

The Author may open the Source Code during Active Development at their own discretion, at any time. This is a gift to the community, not a transfer of copyright.

WHEN THE PROJECT IS ABANDONED

If the Project becomes Abandoned, the Author must open its Source Code to everyone within 30 days of that moment.

The code must be published in a way that allows it to be used: studied, modified, built, and developed further. It must be published under an open source license that at minimum permits use, study, modification, reproduction, distribution, and the creation and distribution of Derivative Works.

The chosen license must preserve the authorship and copyrights of the original Author.

AUTHOR NAME AND PROHIBITION OF SELF-RENUNCIATION

The Author's name is part of the Project itself. Under the WAKE License, voluntarily removing one's own name or making the project anonymous is prohibited. When distributing the Project or a Derivative Work, preserve, where technically possible:

the name or pseudonym of the original Author;
the name of the original Project;
the original copyright notice;
a link to the original Project, if the Author provided one.

You may sign your own changes with your name. But removing, hiding, or distorting the name of the original Author is prohibited. Passing someone else's work off as your own is the most serious violation of this License.

MODIFIED VERSIONS AND NAMES

If you have modified the Project, state this honestly. Do not present your version as the original or as an official version of the Author without their consent.

PERMISSION TO USE

Full — use the license as much as you want without violating the license itself.

License Text — it is not mandatory to distribute the entire text; it is sufficient to state that the Project is licensed under WAKE.

HOW TO SHARE THE PROJECT

When distributing the Project, you:

keep the text of this License or its terms available;
preserve copyright and authorship notices;
do not misrepresent the origin of the Project;
comply with the remaining terms of the License.

You may charge money for distribution, support, hosting, and other services. But payment does not make you the copyright holder.

CONTRIBUTOR (CO-AUTHOR) PROVISION

Any third-party developers submitting improvements (Pull Requests, patches, or code) to the Project agree that during Active Development the sole beneficiary of all sales and incoming donations is the current Lead Author. Contributors have no right to demand a share of the profits unless otherwise agreed in a separate written agreement, however, their names remain in the change history.

IF THE AUTHOR RETURNS AND FORK STATUS

The Author may return to work even after the Project has been recognized as Abandoned and release new versions, including with closed Source Code, returning the Project to the Active Development stage.

Code that was already opened under an open source license during the period of abandonment remains under its terms. The Author cannot take back rights that people have lawfully received under such a license.

Any third party who created a fork of the open code during the period of abandonment has the right to independently choose its further fate: keep the fork open, or close it again under the WAKE 1.0 model, including mandatory donations in their own favor, provided that the name of the original Author is preserved absolutely and inseparably.

WHEN RIGHTS TERMINATE

If you substantially violate the License, your rights under it terminate automatically. If you correct the violation and the law allows it, the rights may be restored.

Those who lawfully received the Project from you do not lose their rights because you lost yours.

AUTHOR'S RIGHTS

All copyrights and other intellectual property rights to the Project belong to the Author, except for the rights expressly granted by this License.

Use, copying, modification, and distribution of the Project do not transfer ownership of it. The License grants the right to use the Project, not to own it.

The Author remains the Author, regardless of what happens to the Project afterwards.

